statement.paragraph:
Let $\textbf{v}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      2 \\
      3 \\
      {- 5}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack,$ $\textbf{v}_{2} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 4} \\
      {- 5} \\
      8
      \end{array} \right\rbrack,$ and $\textbf{w} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      8 \\
      2 \\
      {- 9}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$. Determine if $\mathbf{w}$ is in the subspace of $\mathbf{\mathbb{R}}^{3}$ generated by $\textbf{v}_{1}$ and $\textbf{v}_{2}$.﻿

Let $\textbf{v}_{1} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      2 \\
      {- 8} \\
      6
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\text{,}$ $\textbf{v}_{2} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 3} \\
      8 \\
      {- 7}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\text{,}$ $\textbf{v}_{3} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 4} \\
      6 \\
      {- 7}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\text{,}$ $\textbf{p} = \,\,\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      6 \\
      {- 10} \\
      11
      \end{array} \right\rbrack\text{,}$ and $A = \left\lbrack \mathbf{v}_{1}\,\mathbf{v}_{2}\,\mathbf{v}_{3} \right\rbrack\text{.}$
